      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Matrix algebra provides a powerful approach for analyzing linear combinations of random variables. Let x be a column vector containing n random variables, $ \\mathbf{x} = (x_1, x_2, \\cdots, x_n)^T $. We may wish to construct a new univariate (scalar) random variable y by taking some linear combination of the elements of $ \\mathbf{x} $,",
